Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:20:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/24] Test sticky promotion failures; leave failing repros of
 three suspected defects

A promotion or retiring checkpoint whose data file stops syncing after it
wrote leaves the engine read-only (decision 6): reads return the last
acknowledged rows, writes are refused with the record (the original failure
as inner exception) without changing a file, and the journal stays.

Left failing (suspected engine defects):
- a retiring checkpoint's promotion refused before it writes is recorded as
  a sticky write failure (implementation note 6 says it is not a failure);
- a promotion stopped with its header journal kept records walKept false,
  "The log file was empty.";
- a failed promotion header write records no file.

ReadOnlyAfterWriteFailure.AssertReported takes walKept as bool? (null: not
checked); existing callers are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UFnsmor6qyZMSd1VoKwfJh
